            "description": "Watch Greenville Triumph vs Loudoun United FC highlights and goals from USL Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on June 10, 2026. The atmosphere was thick with anticipation as two determined sides took to the pitch for another high-stakes encounter in the USL Championship . With both teams eager to climb the table, the stage was set for a tactical battle that would keep fans on the edge of their seats. Tactical Discipline in the Opening Period On June 10, 2026 , Greenville Triumph hosted Loudoun United in a fixture that began as a chess match between two well-drilled units. The first half saw both defenses reign supreme, as clear-cut chances remained at a premium. Loudoun United focused on maintaining a compact shape, successfully frustrating the hosts' attempts to build momentum. While Greenville Triumph enjoyed longer spells of possession, they found it difficult to penetrate the final third, leading to a tense and scoreless opening phase of the match . Second Half Breakthrough The dynamic of the contest shifted dramatically following the interval. Greenville Triumph emerged for the second half with renewed energy, pushing their wing-backs higher and testing the visitors' resolve. The pressure finally told in the 64th minute when C. Evans clinical finish extended the lead to 2-0. This goal forced Loudoun United to abandon their defensive posture, creating a more open and expansive game of football as the visitors searched for a way back into the contest. Sealing the Victory and Late Response As the clock ticked down, the home side continued to exploit the gaps left by a tiring defense. In the 85th minute, J. Bouregy effectively put the game out of reach by making it 3-0, much to the delight of the home supporters. Despite the daunting deficit, Loudoun United refused to capitulate entirely. In the third minute of stoppage time (90+3), A. Souper managed to pull one back for the visitors to make it 3-1, though it proved to be nothing more than a late consolation in a dominant performance by the hosts.",
